{"name":"New Riders of the Purple Sage","hex":"#691d6c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"new","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Newar."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Recently made, or created.","Of recent origin; having taken place recently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/new"},{"term":"riders","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of rider"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riders"},{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"}],"entries":[{"title":"New Riders of the Purple Sage","blocks":[{"text":"New Riders of the Purple Sage was an American country rock band. The group emerged from the psychedelic rock scene in San Francisco in 1969 and its original lineup included several members of the Grateful Dead. The band is sometimes referred to as the New Riders or as NRPS."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/New-Riders-of-the-Purple-Sage-01.jpg/330px-New-Riders-of-the-Purple-Sage-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Riders_of_the_Purple_Sage","wikidata":"Q1420833"},{"title":"New Riders of the Purple Sage (album)","blocks":[{"text":"New Riders of the Purple Sage is the debut album by the American country rock band the New Riders of the Purple Sage. It was released by Columbia Records in 1971, and reached number 39 on the Billboard charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/NewRiders1971.jpg?u